            <h2 class="text-white">Interventions</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Physical Literacy interventions aim to reimagine physical education as a tool for holistic development by embedding movement, inclusion, and well-being into the core of school life.</p>
          <ul class="list">
            <li>&quot;Play for All&quot; curriculum is co-developed with the state government for grades 1–12, focusing on Physical Literacy.</li>
            <li>District officials and principals are trained to understand and advocate the importance of Physical Literacy.</li>
            <li>A cadre of Master Facilitators is created to train Physical Education Instructors (PTIs) through ongoing, practical workshops.</li>
            <li>Schools are encouraged to include dedicated sports periods and organize annual sports days to build a culture of physical activity.</li>
            <li>Governance structures are set up within schools to sustain Physical Literacy interventions.</li>
            <li>Advocacy is done for recruiting permanent PTIs and implementing a monitoring and evaluation system.</li>
            <li>The goal is to foster a holistic and sustainable approach to physical education and student well-being.</li>
          </ul>
